# Auto commit and push

This project requires finishing every agent turn that changed files with a git commit and push.

## When to run

At the end of the response, if this conversation made any file changes (or there are uncommitted changes from this work):

1. Run `git status`, `git diff`, and `git log -5 --oneline` in parallel
2. Stage relevant files (never stage secrets like `.env`, credentials)
3. Create a commit with a concise message via HEREDOC (focus on why)
4. Push to the tracked remote with `git push` (or `git push -u origin HEAD` if needed)
5. Tell the user the commit hash/message and that it was pushed

## Rules

- This **overrides** the default “only commit when asked” preference for this repo
- Do not create an empty commit if there is nothing to commit
- Do not use `--force` push unless the user explicitly asks
- Do not amend commits that were already pushed
- Skip only if the user explicitly said not to commit/push in that message

## Commit message style

- 1–2 short sentences
- Prefer verbs like `fix`, `add`, `update`
- Example: `Fix Stream video listing UTF-8 decode so the picker returns videos.`
